# What the website does not need. Everything here stays in the repo - this only
# keeps it from being uploaded to the host and served to anyone who guesses a
# URL, which is what GitHub Pages has been doing with all of it.
#
# The site is index.html, manifest.json, js/ and audio/. Nothing else.

# The phone build: an 11 MB apk, its manifest, its sources and its vendored
# copy of phaser. Built from this repo, never fetched by the browser.
android/

# The small AAC set, for a host with a size cap. This build reads the mp3
# masters - AUDIO_EXT in AudioManager.js says so - so shipping these too would
# be 2.7 MB nobody asks for.
audio-web/

# Build scripts and their outputs.
*.ps1
*.zip

# The single-file bundle. Still built, still what the apk is made from, but the
# site runs from js/ and never loads it.
heartbound.html

# Notes to whoever works on this, not a page.
README.md

# Repo bookkeeping. Harmless, but there is no reason for a visitor to be able
# to fetch them - .gitignore in particular names the signing keystore.
.gitignore
.gitattributes
